00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,611 --> 00:00:07,446
TWO MONTHS EARLIER

2
00:00:07,529 --> 00:00:10,198
[people chattering]

3
00:00:10,282 --> 00:00:12,284
[♪ jazz music playing]

4
00:00:15,829 --> 00:00:17,372
[Geonyoung] <i>They say that in this world,</i>

5
00:00:17,456 --> 00:00:20,125
<i>no one stays your friend</i>
<i>or your enemy forever.</i>

6
00:00:21,877 --> 00:00:24,755
<i>Which means that anyone</i>
<i>can stab you in the back at any moment</i>

7
00:00:24,838 --> 00:00:26,506
<i>for their own personal gain.</i>

8
00:00:27,174 --> 00:00:29,259
<i>There's no telling</i>
<i>when you might be betrayed.</i>

9
00:00:31,219 --> 00:00:34,056
<i>But here's the saying</i>
<i>that rings truer to me right now.</i>

10
00:00:35,307 --> 00:00:38,101
<i>"The enemy of your enemy is your friend."</i>

11
00:00:38,185 --> 00:00:40,395
[patrons chattering]

12
00:00:41,313 --> 00:00:43,482
-[soldier] Sir!
-Sit down, sit down, it's okay.

13
00:00:43,565 --> 00:00:45,150
At ease, guys. At ease. Sit down.

14
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:46,401
[Geonyoung] Colonel Ahn.

15
00:00:48,236 --> 00:00:49,821
[Jaeho] Sorry I'm late.

16
00:00:49,905 --> 00:00:51,907
It's fine. Haven't been here long.

17
00:00:51,990 --> 00:00:54,743
Can you believe it's so hot
at this time of night?

18
00:00:54,826 --> 00:00:56,078
[Geonyoung] Tell me about it.

19
00:00:56,661 --> 00:00:59,539
-I appreciate you showing up, Colonel.
-[chuckles]

20
00:00:59,623 --> 00:01:02,292
If you call me, Geonyoung,
then I come running.

21
00:01:02,376 --> 00:01:04,419
-Excuse me?
-Yeah?

22
00:01:04,503 --> 00:01:06,505
Two bowls of gukbap
and one order of suyuk please.

23
00:01:06,588 --> 00:01:07,589
[cook] You got it.

24
00:01:08,423 --> 00:01:09,925
-You're drinking, right?
-Yeah, sure.

25
00:01:10,008 --> 00:01:11,927
-Here.
-Oh, uh…

26
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:13,762
It's hot out,
I'm gonna get a beer instead.

27
00:01:13,845 --> 00:01:15,013
All right.

28
00:01:16,556 --> 00:01:17,599
[clears throat]

29
00:01:18,725 --> 00:01:20,644
-[Jaeho] Can I grab a beer?
-[cook] Sure.

30
00:01:23,355 --> 00:01:24,690
[Jaeho] Here, you want some?

31
00:01:25,899 --> 00:01:28,235
I always tried to see you
at the prosecutor's office,

32
00:01:28,318 --> 00:01:29,319
but you avoided me.

33
00:01:31,405 --> 00:01:34,199
Yeah, that's why I wound up
an unemployed loser,

34
00:01:34,282 --> 00:01:36,702
and you turned into a bigwig
of national security.

35
00:01:36,785 --> 00:01:39,913
Oh, come on now.
You know, ever since high school,

36
00:01:40,497 --> 00:01:43,583
I've just been trying to catch up to you,
and I'm still way behind.

37
00:01:43,667 --> 00:01:45,502
[Geonyoung chuckling]

38
00:01:53,969 --> 00:01:55,178
Ah, that's nice.

39
00:01:55,929 --> 00:01:57,597
When I heard about you,

40
00:01:58,223 --> 00:02:01,017
I was wondering how you were doing
and what you might be up to.

41
00:02:01,101 --> 00:02:03,687
-[chuckles]
-You should've reached out sooner.

42
00:02:04,479 --> 00:02:06,648
You think I wouldn't be able
to help you out?

43
00:02:07,691 --> 00:02:09,818
So what have you been doing all this time?

44
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:12,279
I mean, what options did I really have?

45
00:02:12,362 --> 00:02:14,823
[chuckles] You know
those Gangnam apartments?

46
00:02:14,906 --> 00:02:17,325
-I worked on all those.
-You worked construction?

47
00:02:17,409 --> 00:02:20,328
[chuckles] Not a lot of options
for an ex-con.

48
00:02:20,412 --> 00:02:23,957
Sometimes you take crappy jobs
to put food on the table.

49
00:02:24,583 --> 00:02:26,209
[chuckling]

50
00:02:27,461 --> 00:02:29,546
-Well, thanks. [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

51
00:02:33,383 --> 00:02:34,509
[sighs]

52
00:02:36,011 --> 00:02:37,137
Ah, that's good.

53
00:02:38,305 --> 00:02:39,473
Mmm. [sniffles]

54
00:02:41,099 --> 00:02:42,100
[Jaeho] Oh.

55
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:46,688
Your hand…

56
00:02:48,023 --> 00:02:51,651
Yeah, I hurt it a little.
I, uh, can't straighten it anymore.

57
00:02:51,735 --> 00:02:53,904
-[laughs]
-Oh, wow.

58
00:02:53,987 --> 00:02:56,198
Guess I'm an invalid now.

59
00:03:00,619 --> 00:03:01,870
[sighs]

60
00:03:05,832 --> 00:03:07,167
What's in the bag?

61
00:03:07,250 --> 00:03:11,046
Well, I had to have
something to show after all these years.

62
00:03:11,588 --> 00:03:12,631
Take a look.

63
00:03:15,801 --> 00:03:16,802
[clears throat]

64
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:22,140
PERSONAL RECORD: BAEK KITAE
PERSONAL RECORD: CHEON SEOKJUNG

65
00:03:22,224 --> 00:03:23,266
Chief Cheon Seokjung.

66
00:03:24,392 --> 00:03:25,894
His slush fund records.

67
00:03:26,686 --> 00:03:28,063
It's 70 billion won.

68
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:32,192
[♪ tense music playing]

69
00:03:33,610 --> 00:03:35,946
Seventy billion?

70
00:03:37,864 --> 00:03:39,199
BAEKHO TRADING CEO BAEK SOYEONG

71
00:03:41,868 --> 00:03:44,454
You and your agency can't
just serve as lackeys

72
00:03:44,538 --> 00:03:46,248
for the KCIA forever, right?

73
00:03:47,707 --> 00:03:49,709
You should take advantage
of your opportunities.

74
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:53,505
Oh, we're their lackeys? [chuckles]

75
00:03:56,424 --> 00:03:57,842
When did you

76
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,096
have time to do all of this?

77
00:04:01,179 --> 00:04:02,430
It wasn't that long.

78
00:04:03,348 --> 00:04:04,975
Just took seven years. [chuckles]

79
00:04:05,767 --> 00:04:07,477
[dog barking in distance]

80
00:04:07,561 --> 00:04:09,563
[♪ music continues]

81
00:04:26,913 --> 00:04:29,165
[blows nose, sniffles]

82
00:04:46,391 --> 00:04:47,475
[sighs]

83
00:04:47,559 --> 00:04:48,768
[fire crackling]

84
00:04:48,852 --> 00:04:50,020
<i>Now,</i>

85
00:04:51,229 --> 00:04:53,440
I want you to swear you'll do one thing.

86
00:04:53,523 --> 00:04:54,691
Tell me what it is.

87
00:04:54,774 --> 00:04:57,736
Once you take down Cheon Seokjung
and Baek Kitae, promise me

88
00:04:58,612 --> 00:05:00,405
you'll help me get my old job back.

89
00:05:03,074 --> 00:05:05,452
I can't live as an ex-con
for the rest of my life.

90
00:05:06,995 --> 00:05:08,413
Can I?

91
00:05:08,496 --> 00:05:09,497
I'm shocked

92
00:05:10,874 --> 00:05:13,293
by how much you've changed. [chuckles]

93
00:05:16,296 --> 00:05:17,547
-[glasses clink]
-[chuckles]

94
00:05:17,631 --> 00:05:19,132
[♪ theme music playing]

95
00:06:13,687 --> 00:06:15,271
SPECIAL ADVISOR JANG GEONYOUNG

96
00:06:15,355 --> 00:06:16,815
[lighter flicks open]

97
00:06:18,358 --> 00:06:19,442
[exhales]

98
00:06:19,526 --> 00:06:20,777
[lighter strikes]

99
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:27,117
Ah, I'm glad you're here, Colonel Baek.

100
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,994
-[Jaeho] Good afternoon, sir.
-[door closes]

101
00:06:30,203 --> 00:06:32,163
-You been waiting long?
-[Jaeho] He just got here.

102
00:06:34,791 --> 00:06:36,167
[Geonyoung] Well, take a seat.

103
00:06:37,585 --> 00:06:39,212
[♪ tense music playing]

104
00:06:40,213 --> 00:06:41,214
Baek, go ahead.

105
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:42,966
Take a seat.

106
00:06:45,051 --> 00:06:46,344
[Geonyoung sighs]

107
00:06:46,928 --> 00:06:49,389
All right, let's see,
do I have everything?

108
00:06:49,472 --> 00:06:50,932
[papers rustling]

109
00:06:55,186 --> 00:06:56,312
Oh, thanks.

110
00:06:59,107 --> 00:07:02,777
Two soldiers… [grunts] …ought
to share a few smokes, am I right?

111
00:07:03,361 --> 00:07:04,362
Huh?

112
00:07:05,196 --> 00:07:06,573
Here. Oh.

113
00:07:08,575 --> 00:07:10,410
-Mmm.
-What are you doing? Don't be rude.

114
00:07:21,546 --> 00:07:23,882
Well, Colonel Baek,
I'm excited to work with you.

115
00:07:24,674 --> 00:07:27,969
Starting tomorrow,
you'll be reporting here.

116
00:07:28,052 --> 00:07:31,014
Help him. Give him the support he needs.

117
00:07:32,932 --> 00:07:36,394
We should go grab lunch together.
After all, we're a team now.

118
00:07:36,478 --> 00:07:37,479
[Jaeho] Sounds good.

119
00:07:38,229 --> 00:07:40,190
[phone ringing]

120
00:07:40,273 --> 00:07:41,608
Mmm. Excuse me.

121
00:07:48,156 --> 00:07:49,532
This is Jang Geonyoung.

122
00:07:49,616 --> 00:07:51,618
[♪ music continues]

123
00:07:58,583 --> 00:08:00,585
[Geonyoung exhales deeply]

124
00:08:07,342 --> 00:08:10,011
IKEDA YUJI …70 BILLION THROUGH
BAEKHO TRADING FROM 1974 TO 1979

125
00:08:10,678 --> 00:08:11,721
[sighs]

126
00:08:13,723 --> 00:08:14,974
Baek, I'm sorry,

127
00:08:15,934 --> 00:08:19,354
but we'll have to have lunch
some other day.

128
00:08:21,689 --> 00:08:22,690
I've got to head out.

129
00:08:24,734 --> 00:08:26,778
[whispers] Make sure
he doesn't call anyone.

130
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:33,201
Well, Colonel, we'll see you tomorrow.

131
00:08:35,286 --> 00:08:37,914
Uh, by all means,
take your time and finish your cigarette.

132
00:08:38,748 --> 00:08:41,543
-[Jaeho] All right. See you later, sir.
-Mm-hmm.

133
00:09:07,944 --> 00:09:09,946
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

134
00:09:21,291 --> 00:09:22,584
Open fire!

135
00:09:56,993 --> 00:09:57,994
[knocks]

136
00:09:58,077 --> 00:09:59,621
[Geonyoung] Mr. Baek Kitae.

137
00:10:07,503 --> 00:10:08,922
Long time no see.

138
00:10:10,632 --> 00:10:11,633
What the…

139
00:10:12,759 --> 00:10:15,136
I'm a special advisor to the JIH.

140
00:10:18,973 --> 00:10:20,433
Ikeda Yuji.

141
00:10:20,516 --> 00:10:22,185
Or should I say, Choi Yuji.

142
00:10:23,561 --> 00:10:25,230
You two haven't changed at all.

143
00:10:26,439 --> 00:10:28,566
What the hell are you up to? What is this?

144
00:10:28,650 --> 00:10:31,402
What's it look like? I'm doing my job.

145
00:10:32,862 --> 00:10:35,156
-Get her out of the car.
-[door opens]

146
00:10:36,074 --> 00:10:37,492
[Kitae] Get your hands off her. Hey!

147
00:10:39,661 --> 00:10:41,412
What do you think you're doing? [spits]

148
00:10:42,038 --> 00:10:44,123
You assholes don't know who I am, huh?

149
00:10:44,624 --> 00:10:46,042
We're on orders from General Hwang.

150
00:10:46,125 --> 00:10:49,170
He received a tip
concerning national security.

151
00:10:49,254 --> 00:10:51,005
Please cooperate, Director Baek.

152
00:10:51,547 --> 00:10:52,924
What tip, soldier?

153
00:10:53,007 --> 00:10:56,302
That a member of the Yakuza
is smuggling 70 billion won in cash

154
00:10:56,386 --> 00:10:57,553
into the country.

155
00:10:58,429 --> 00:11:02,558
And now the acting KCIA director just
happens to be riding in a car with her.

156
00:11:03,268 --> 00:11:04,394
So then…

157
00:11:05,478 --> 00:11:07,897
how about me and you
have a chat later in private?

158
00:11:09,649 --> 00:11:10,692
Listen to me.

159
00:11:11,276 --> 00:11:13,945
You're going to go wait quietly
at the KCIA.

160
00:11:15,071 --> 00:11:17,907
Unless you want bigger problems with me.

161
00:11:17,991 --> 00:11:19,200
What…

162
00:11:21,536 --> 00:11:23,121
you gonna shoot the director?

163
00:11:34,882 --> 00:11:37,802
Let's go.
There's no reason to pick a fight.

164
00:11:37,885 --> 00:11:40,054
-We'll talk at the station.
-Take her away!

165
00:11:41,139 --> 00:11:42,265
Get the money.

166
00:11:42,348 --> 00:11:44,100
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

167
00:12:21,971 --> 00:12:23,765
[Kitae muttering] Son of a bitch.

168
00:12:27,226 --> 00:12:28,311
Damn it!

169
00:12:36,903 --> 00:12:38,321
[huffs]

170
00:12:40,948 --> 00:12:43,576
[Haksu] <i>They took Choi Yuji to the</i>
<i>Joint Investigation Headquarters, and--</i>

171
00:12:43,659 --> 00:12:44,744
What about the money?

172
00:12:46,287 --> 00:12:47,455
<i>They took all of it.</i>

173
00:12:53,544 --> 00:12:56,255
DEPUTY DIRECTOR PYO HAKSU

174
00:12:56,339 --> 00:12:57,632
What a shit show.

175
00:13:02,136 --> 00:13:04,097
Those fucking bastards.

176
00:13:05,098 --> 00:13:06,474
At least it's not me.

177
00:13:11,979 --> 00:13:14,941
[Geonyoung] <i>They can talk all they want</i>
<i>about constitutional reform</i>

178
00:13:15,024 --> 00:13:16,943
<i>and direct presidential elections,</i>

179
00:13:17,527 --> 00:13:21,280
<i>but in the end, the only thing</i>
<i>that changes the world is money.</i>

180
00:13:21,364 --> 00:13:23,074
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

181
00:13:26,661 --> 00:13:27,662
Bitches!

182
00:13:27,745 --> 00:13:29,455
[Geonyoung] <i>Politics is no different</i>
<i>than business.</i>

183
00:13:29,539 --> 00:13:30,540
[screams]

184
00:13:30,623 --> 00:13:33,668
[Geonyoung] <i>Trust, confidence,</i>
<i>loyalty, even people…</i>

185
00:13:33,751 --> 00:13:37,296
<i>at the end of the day, all of these things</i>
<i>can be bought with money.</i>

186
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,923
[panting]

187
00:13:40,091 --> 00:13:42,343
[Geonyoung] <i>The money</i>
<i>I intercepted from Baek Kitae</i>

188
00:13:42,969 --> 00:13:46,389
<i>was supposed to secure the presidency</i>
<i>for Cheon Seokjung.</i>

189
00:13:48,891 --> 00:13:50,393
<i>But now, I'm going to take it</i>

190
00:13:50,935 --> 00:13:52,520
<i>and use it as a weapon.</i>

191
00:13:52,603 --> 00:13:54,438
<i>It's finally time</i>

192
00:13:54,522 --> 00:13:56,482
<i>to go for my enemies' throats.</i>

193
00:14:00,778 --> 00:14:02,864
[chuckles]

194
00:14:10,329 --> 00:14:11,789
Wow.

195
00:14:11,873 --> 00:14:13,583
Seventy billion.

196
00:14:14,667 --> 00:14:17,003
Baek lined his pockets, huh?

197
00:14:17,086 --> 00:14:18,087
If it weren't for you,

198
00:14:18,171 --> 00:14:21,215
it looks like he would've
sucked the whole country dry eventually.

199
00:14:21,299 --> 00:14:22,425
[Geonyoung chuckles]

200
00:14:22,508 --> 00:14:25,052
I wonder what exactly

201
00:14:25,636 --> 00:14:27,471
his plan was here, you know?

202
00:14:27,555 --> 00:14:31,350
Cheon Seokjung had
to have some larger end goal.

203
00:14:31,893 --> 00:14:34,687
I mean, how would you even spend this?

204
00:14:35,271 --> 00:14:37,732
Baek Kitae wants to swallow
this country whole.

205
00:14:38,608 --> 00:14:40,818
-In one go.
-[scoffs]

206
00:14:41,319 --> 00:14:44,363
That sneaky, thieving little bastard.

207
00:14:44,447 --> 00:14:47,783
We have targets now.
Baekho Trading is first.

208
00:14:47,867 --> 00:14:49,994
And then Cheon Seokjung's slush fund

209
00:14:50,828 --> 00:14:52,914
will be tied to Baek's meth operation.

210
00:14:52,997 --> 00:14:55,875
Which means that we can
destroy them for good.

211
00:14:55,958 --> 00:14:57,043
Uh…

212
00:14:58,169 --> 00:15:01,297
that's going to be… pretty difficult.

213
00:15:04,175 --> 00:15:07,011
We haven't had a memorial service
for the president yet.

214
00:15:07,094 --> 00:15:08,095
Hang on.

215
00:15:09,347 --> 00:15:12,266
What does that have to do
with taking down Baek?

216
00:15:12,850 --> 00:15:16,103
Bringing him down is fine,
but it's the meth…

217
00:15:16,187 --> 00:15:18,606
-It's gonna look bad.
-[scoffs]

218
00:15:19,982 --> 00:15:21,943
Uh, I'm confused.
What do you mean by that?

219
00:15:22,693 --> 00:15:24,445
We're after him because he's dealing meth.

220
00:15:24,528 --> 00:15:27,156
[laughing]

221
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,617
Ah, somehow you're still not getting it.

222
00:15:31,369 --> 00:15:33,496
Jang, look. Think about this for a second.

223
00:15:33,579 --> 00:15:36,999
If it gets out that the men closest
to the president were pushing drugs,

224
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,127
how do you think
the public's going to respond?

225
00:15:41,212 --> 00:15:44,048
Essentially, it would end up
with the president's name

226
00:15:44,131 --> 00:15:45,299
being dragged through the mud.

227
00:15:45,383 --> 00:15:49,679
We have to preserve the legacy
of this country's leadership, don't we?

228
00:15:49,762 --> 00:15:52,556
He's a drug pusher
and he'll pay the price. Simple as that.

229
00:15:56,435 --> 00:15:57,436
General Hwang.

230
00:15:58,813 --> 00:16:00,356
We have an opportunity

231
00:16:00,439 --> 00:16:03,359
to make it clear to the public
how we deal with criminals.

232
00:16:03,442 --> 00:16:06,821
This is how we root them out
and get rid of drug pushers for good.

233
00:16:07,697 --> 00:16:10,116
This is how we preserve
our country's legacy and protect--

234
00:16:10,199 --> 00:16:12,326
All right,
I understand what you're saying.

235
00:16:13,577 --> 00:16:17,415
Let's just circle back to this after
the president's official memorial service.

236
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:21,419
For now, leave the meth out of it
and bring him down with the money.

237
00:16:21,502 --> 00:16:24,255
Look, we have plenty of it
right in front of us, don't we?

238
00:16:26,007 --> 00:16:27,466
That'll keep things…

239
00:16:27,550 --> 00:16:30,177
-[sighs]
-…nice and squeaky clean.

240
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,061
[Haksu] You all right?

241
00:16:39,687 --> 00:16:41,897
What happened to Choi? Did you find out?

242
00:16:42,398 --> 00:16:43,983
[Haksu] Mmm, well…

243
00:16:45,526 --> 00:16:48,112
they took her to the JIH
to interrogate her.

244
00:16:48,904 --> 00:16:50,197
Can you believe that?

245
00:16:51,282 --> 00:16:53,409
Jang Geonyoung teamed up with those guys.

246
00:16:55,202 --> 00:16:56,746
Never thought I'd live to see that.

247
00:16:57,330 --> 00:16:58,414
And the money?

248
00:16:59,498 --> 00:17:01,917
I assume
they'll be holding onto it for a while.

249
00:17:05,796 --> 00:17:06,839
All done.

250
00:17:08,507 --> 00:17:09,717
[Kitae sighs]

251
00:17:10,968 --> 00:17:12,136
The good news is…

252
00:17:14,263 --> 00:17:16,474
they still don't have
any hard evidence yet.

253
00:17:17,892 --> 00:17:20,394
They can't do much
with that kind of money right away.

254
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:22,730
As long as Choi doesn't start blabbing.

255
00:17:24,607 --> 00:17:25,775
[lighter thuds]

256
00:17:25,858 --> 00:17:28,110
How do you think
Jang Geonyoung knew where to go?

257
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:32,448
There's gotta be a leak.

258
00:17:33,074 --> 00:17:35,368
From Japan, or someone who works with us.

259
00:17:38,245 --> 00:17:39,372
[sighs]

260
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:45,586
So, do you think Choi can hold out?

261
00:17:46,921 --> 00:17:49,256
-They'll probably put her through hell.
-[knock on door]

262
00:17:49,924 --> 00:17:51,050
[door opens]

263
00:17:55,221 --> 00:17:56,764
[sighs] Get out.

264
00:18:02,103 --> 00:18:03,187
Hey.

265
00:18:03,896 --> 00:18:05,564
I expect you to greet me, asshole.

266
00:18:08,484 --> 00:18:09,568
Just say…

267
00:18:10,277 --> 00:18:11,320
Piece of shit.

268
00:18:20,162 --> 00:18:21,163
[door closes]

269
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,842
I did a thorough sweep, sir.

270
00:18:33,592 --> 00:18:35,010
There were no bugs.

271
00:18:35,094 --> 00:18:37,054
There's nothing to be concerned about.

272
00:18:38,222 --> 00:18:40,057
Put a few guys on Pyo Haksu.

273
00:18:42,226 --> 00:18:45,813
I want a report on everything,
everyone he meets.

274
00:18:45,896 --> 00:18:47,440
Of course, sir. I'm on it.

275
00:18:50,735 --> 00:18:52,153
Takahashi Kazuo.

276
00:18:52,236 --> 00:18:54,822
He's stuck by Choi Yuji's side
for ten years.

277
00:18:54,905 --> 00:18:57,825
My guess is, he's been holding onto
the ledger for a while.

278
00:18:57,908 --> 00:18:58,909
PERSONAL RECORD

279
00:18:58,993 --> 00:19:00,953
Knowing Yuji,
there's no way she'd keep the money

280
00:19:01,036 --> 00:19:02,663
and the ledger in the same place.

281
00:19:03,456 --> 00:19:06,083
If that ledger gets found
by anybody in the JIH,

282
00:19:06,709 --> 00:19:08,669
we'll be dead. So go find him now.

283
00:19:09,378 --> 00:19:10,504
Copy that.

284
00:19:15,176 --> 00:19:16,469
[door opens]

285
00:19:30,149 --> 00:19:31,984
-[phone ringing]
-[faint chattering]

286
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:44,955
-A yakuza from Osaka named Choi Yuji.
-Yeah?

287
00:19:59,178 --> 00:20:00,554
[Kihyun] Section Chief Park.

288
00:20:02,473 --> 00:20:05,309
Yeah? I got it.

289
00:20:06,602 --> 00:20:07,770
How have you been, sir?

290
00:20:08,479 --> 00:20:10,689
Oh. Baek, what are you doing here?

291
00:20:10,773 --> 00:20:13,317
I received an assignment here
that begins this morning.

292
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,944
-I'm looking forward to--
-[chuckling] Oh, no.

293
00:20:15,027 --> 00:20:17,154
Come on, you didn't have to do this.

294
00:20:17,947 --> 00:20:19,240
All right, thanks.

295
00:20:19,990 --> 00:20:21,408
You have any questions, let me know.

296
00:20:21,492 --> 00:20:23,077
Thanks, sir. Much appreciated.

297
00:20:24,495 --> 00:20:25,663
Oh, Baek.

298
00:20:26,413 --> 00:20:27,498
Yes, sir?

299
00:20:29,542 --> 00:20:30,835
Did you hear about it?

300
00:20:30,918 --> 00:20:32,127
Hear about what?

301
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:34,338
Ikeda Yuji, we caught her.

302
00:20:34,421 --> 00:20:36,215
Word is she's a member of the Yakuza.

303
00:20:36,799 --> 00:20:37,925
Why was she brought in?

304
00:20:38,008 --> 00:20:41,262
She brought money into Busan illegally.
And lots of it.

305
00:20:41,345 --> 00:20:42,763
[sighs] How much?

306
00:20:47,518 --> 00:20:48,894
Seventy billion.

307
00:20:50,187 --> 00:20:53,065
Just imagine how many cartons
70 billion would buy you.

308
00:20:53,148 --> 00:20:54,984
[♪ intriguing music playing]

309
00:20:55,067 --> 00:20:57,444
[sighs] Anyway, thanks for these.

310
00:20:58,028 --> 00:20:59,613
-Sure.
-[blows]

311
00:21:00,322 --> 00:21:02,324
[typewriter keys clacking]

312
00:21:16,714 --> 00:21:18,799
[investigator] Oh, good morning, ma'am.

313
00:21:19,717 --> 00:21:22,845
Miss Oh, a Yakuza woman named Choi Yuji

314
00:21:22,928 --> 00:21:25,139
got busted for smuggling 70 billion won.

315
00:21:25,222 --> 00:21:26,223
Seventy billion?

316
00:21:26,307 --> 00:21:28,267
Yeah, it's making waves in the department.

317
00:21:51,081 --> 00:21:52,082
[door closes]

318
00:21:53,834 --> 00:21:55,502
Choi Yuji. You brought her in here?

319
00:21:56,128 --> 00:21:57,171
Yes.

320
00:21:59,131 --> 00:22:00,341
-[sighs]
-Hey, you

321
00:22:00,424 --> 00:22:03,177
could've told me about this beforehand.

322
00:22:04,678 --> 00:22:06,472
Why exactly would I do that?

323
00:22:07,056 --> 00:22:08,390
What good would that do?

324
00:22:11,143 --> 00:22:12,519
Well, never mind.

325
00:22:19,026 --> 00:22:22,029
The raw materials for their meth
came in from Taiwan.

326
00:22:23,906 --> 00:22:25,741
So I'm gonna get a warrant

327
00:22:25,824 --> 00:22:28,327
for Baek Soyeong, now that we have proof.

328
00:22:30,371 --> 00:22:31,872
[sighs]

329
00:22:33,666 --> 00:22:34,708
You wanna give it a shot?

330
00:22:35,668 --> 00:22:37,211
Take a crack at Choi Yuji?

331
00:22:37,753 --> 00:22:38,754
Really?

332
00:22:40,756 --> 00:22:41,757
Mmm.

333
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:46,011
[Yejin] Miss Choi Yuji.

334
00:22:47,054 --> 00:22:49,765
Why did you smuggle
70 billion won into Korea?

335
00:22:49,848 --> 00:22:52,101
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

336
00:22:52,184 --> 00:22:53,894
Did Baek Kitae put you up to it?

337
00:22:55,729 --> 00:22:57,815
[screaming in distance]

338
00:23:00,484 --> 00:23:04,405
All of that money
came from selling meth, isn't that right?

339
00:23:05,614 --> 00:23:08,826
And then you went and laundered it
into Chief Cheon's slush fund.

340
00:23:09,702 --> 00:23:10,995
[door opens]

341
00:23:12,413 --> 00:23:15,165
[Yejin on speakers] <i>Hey, Miss Choi.</i>
<i>What, can't you talk?</i>

342
00:23:20,212 --> 00:23:22,464
<i>You're just gonna keep your mouth shut?</i>

343
00:23:22,548 --> 00:23:23,549
[chuckles]

344
00:23:23,632 --> 00:23:25,884
[Yejin] You clearly don't understand
the situation you're in.

345
00:23:26,635 --> 00:23:29,221
Yeah, you probably think
the whole world just turns for you

346
00:23:29,304 --> 00:23:30,431
with a face like that.

347
00:23:31,056 --> 00:23:33,976
[scoffs] You got another thing coming.

348
00:23:35,227 --> 00:23:37,896
[chuckles]
Yeah, and how would you know?

349
00:23:38,397 --> 00:23:39,398
Moron.

350
00:23:39,898 --> 00:23:41,525
-[Yejin]<i> What?</i>
-[slurping loudly]

351
00:23:42,359 --> 00:23:44,236
[Yejin] <i>"Moron?" Hey.</i>

352
00:23:47,197 --> 00:23:48,741
<i>Listen to me carefully.</i>

353
00:23:51,243 --> 00:23:53,746
Right now, Korea's under martial law.

354
00:23:53,829 --> 00:23:56,415
So the military controls
the whole country.

355
00:23:56,498 --> 00:23:57,916
Got it?

356
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:00,252
You know what that means
for your situation?

357
00:24:01,420 --> 00:24:02,421
What's your point?

358
00:24:03,213 --> 00:24:04,465
You think I care?

359
00:24:05,507 --> 00:24:06,717
You know I'm Japanese, right?

360
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:08,427
[exclaims]

361
00:24:08,510 --> 00:24:11,930
That makes no fucking difference!
Doesn't mean a damn thing!

362
00:24:12,639 --> 00:24:15,642
<i>Are you listening?</i>
<i>I said Korea is under martial law.</i>

363
00:24:15,726 --> 00:24:19,021
Which means
everything is different right now.

364
00:24:19,104 --> 00:24:21,857
And nobody in this country
is playing by the rules anymore.

365
00:24:22,983 --> 00:24:26,153
It doesn't matter where you're from,
'cause you're not in Japan!

366
00:24:26,236 --> 00:24:27,863
You're in Korea!

367
00:24:27,946 --> 00:24:31,450
If you're not careful,
a little yakuza girl like you

368
00:24:31,533 --> 00:24:33,160
could wind up dead in no time.

369
00:24:33,243 --> 00:24:35,662
-[snickering]
-Is that funny?

370
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:40,584
Yeah. All right, I get it.

371
00:24:44,421 --> 00:24:47,007
-Just give me a smoke, okay?
-What?

372
00:24:48,509 --> 00:24:50,135
You little bitch.

373
00:24:52,262 --> 00:24:54,264
[humming]

374
00:24:54,348 --> 00:24:56,350
[faint screaming]

375
00:24:59,978 --> 00:25:01,772
[doors bang]

376
00:25:02,940 --> 00:25:03,982
[sighs]

377
00:25:04,066 --> 00:25:05,692
[faint screaming continues]

378
00:25:15,536 --> 00:25:17,121
[sighs]

379
00:25:35,597 --> 00:25:39,601
I bet you think you and Baek Kitae

380
00:25:41,186 --> 00:25:42,813
are gonna last forever.

381
00:25:45,482 --> 00:25:47,776
You've shared a bed… [exhales sharply]

382
00:25:49,194 --> 00:25:50,863
…you've shared your money…

383
00:25:53,282 --> 00:25:55,701
You two have shared everything. Right?

384
00:25:56,326 --> 00:26:00,622
I mean, a pair of drug pushers
in love with each other?

385
00:26:01,790 --> 00:26:04,209
That's pretty crazy. Right?

386
00:26:04,293 --> 00:26:05,961
Not very romantic, is it?

387
00:26:06,044 --> 00:26:08,088
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

388
00:26:09,882 --> 00:26:12,467
Hey, am I wrong about you two?

389
00:26:13,760 --> 00:26:15,262
So the ledger

390
00:26:17,181 --> 00:26:19,391
for Cheon's 70 billion won fund.

391
00:26:20,267 --> 00:26:21,935
If you can get it for me,

392
00:26:23,604 --> 00:26:25,355
you'll walk out of here alive.

393
00:26:26,106 --> 00:26:27,191
Hmm?

394
00:26:32,321 --> 00:26:34,531
I have Japanese papers, sir.

395
00:26:35,407 --> 00:26:37,659
Contact the embassy, they'll sort it out.

396
00:26:38,911 --> 00:26:41,205
The prosecutor told you
nobody cares about that.

397
00:26:41,288 --> 00:26:42,539
Were you not listening?

398
00:26:43,498 --> 00:26:44,917
Don't give me that crap.

399
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:48,086
The country's under martial law.
You know you're screwed.

400
00:26:49,796 --> 00:26:52,132
Tell me where I can find it. The ledger.

401
00:26:55,636 --> 00:26:57,763
I have Japanese papers, sir.

402
00:26:59,306 --> 00:27:01,183
Please contact the embassy.

403
00:27:03,477 --> 00:27:04,519
[Geonyoung scoffs]

404
00:27:05,854 --> 00:27:07,064
Listen, smart-ass.

405
00:27:07,564 --> 00:27:09,149
[faint screaming continues]

406
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:11,401
Do you hear that?

407
00:27:12,069 --> 00:27:13,695
[screaming intensifies]

408
00:27:14,988 --> 00:27:16,949
Really, can you hear that? Are you deaf?

409
00:27:17,032 --> 00:27:19,201
[high-pitched screaming]

410
00:27:22,829 --> 00:27:24,081
You're a criminal.

411
00:27:28,669 --> 00:27:30,128
Okay, tough guy.

412
00:27:30,212 --> 00:27:31,380
Now you listen to me.

413
00:27:32,381 --> 00:27:33,632
You have two choices.

414
00:27:34,883 --> 00:27:37,970
You either die and vanish in here,
or you walk out alive.

415
00:27:40,889 --> 00:27:42,808
Where's the slush fund ledger?

416
00:27:42,891 --> 00:27:44,393
[♪ music continues]

417
00:27:50,816 --> 00:27:51,900
[scoffs]

418
00:28:07,624 --> 00:28:09,292
[bucket rattles]

419
00:28:12,796 --> 00:28:14,047
[Geonyoung] Get in here!

420
00:28:16,967 --> 00:28:18,051
Tie her up.

421
00:28:39,156 --> 00:28:40,782
You staying, Prosecutor Oh?

422
00:28:42,492 --> 00:28:44,369
You can leave if you don't wanna watch.

423
00:28:54,504 --> 00:28:55,547
[sighs]

424
00:28:58,050 --> 00:28:59,134
Choi Yuji.

425
00:28:59,217 --> 00:29:02,345
The ledger for Cheon's slush fund,
tell me where it is.

426
00:29:02,429 --> 00:29:03,597
Right now.

427
00:29:05,766 --> 00:29:07,434
[faint screaming]

428
00:29:16,735 --> 00:29:19,905
Kitae, I have a feeling
the KCIA is crawling with rats.

429
00:29:21,615 --> 00:29:22,824
Isn't it?

430
00:29:28,288 --> 00:29:30,332
How the hell did they know where to go?

431
00:29:32,918 --> 00:29:33,919
Sir, it's my fault.

432
00:29:38,799 --> 00:29:40,008
[Seokjung] Now what?

433
00:29:41,843 --> 00:29:44,971
We're just gonna let someone else
walk away with all of it?

434
00:29:45,806 --> 00:29:48,975
Without the money, that shit heel
Hwang Daesik is gonna string us up

435
00:29:49,059 --> 00:29:50,685
from the nearest tree as soon as he can.

436
00:29:50,769 --> 00:29:52,729
I'll put everything back in order.

437
00:29:52,813 --> 00:29:54,106
Just give me more time.

438
00:29:54,189 --> 00:29:55,941
Are fucking kidding me?

439
00:29:57,859 --> 00:29:58,860
[sighs]

440
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:06,076
I hear your brother joined
the Joint Investigation Headquarters.

441
00:30:07,410 --> 00:30:08,411
[sighs]

442
00:30:12,249 --> 00:30:13,375
What, you…

443
00:30:14,626 --> 00:30:15,961
you weren't aware?

444
00:30:16,711 --> 00:30:17,754
[scoffs]

445
00:30:18,964 --> 00:30:21,216
You don't talk
to your own brother anymore?

446
00:30:21,299 --> 00:30:22,425
[sighs]

447
00:30:24,594 --> 00:30:25,887
Can you really…

448
00:30:27,973 --> 00:30:29,307
trust him after this?

449
00:30:29,391 --> 00:30:32,060
My brother is not going to be a problem.

450
00:30:32,144 --> 00:30:35,480
When it comes down to it,
and you're fighting for money and power…

451
00:30:36,189 --> 00:30:37,190
[scoffs]

452
00:30:38,692 --> 00:30:40,360
…sharing blood is meaningless.

453
00:30:43,822 --> 00:30:45,949
BAEKHO TRADING
ORGANIZATION CHART

454
00:30:46,032 --> 00:30:48,743
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

455
00:30:48,827 --> 00:30:51,163
-[chattering]
-[phone ringing]

456
00:30:51,246 --> 00:30:53,498
[typewriter keys clacking]

457
00:30:56,293 --> 00:30:58,336
-Chief.
-What is it?

458
00:30:58,420 --> 00:31:02,257
[investigator] This guy here,
he's a junior from my neighborhood.

459
00:31:04,885 --> 00:31:06,428
So what was Hwang's response?

460
00:31:07,387 --> 00:31:08,513
[sighs]

461
00:31:08,597 --> 00:31:10,182
He can't be persuaded.

462
00:31:10,265 --> 00:31:12,684
He's the most stubborn bastard
I've ever met.

463
00:31:13,351 --> 00:31:15,687
-[sighs]
-And we haven't

464
00:31:16,479 --> 00:31:18,773
even had a service for the president yet.

465
00:31:18,857 --> 00:31:21,318
-Slow down. Let's pull back a little.
-[scoffs]

466
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:24,613
Look, sir.

467
00:31:25,864 --> 00:31:28,867
[sighs] We're military men. Soldiers.

468
00:31:29,409 --> 00:31:31,453
Our job is to obey orders.

469
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:34,831
You've been around the block.
You should know that by now.

470
00:31:35,498 --> 00:31:36,499
Well,

471
00:31:38,126 --> 00:31:39,753
I should probably get back to work.

472
00:31:39,836 --> 00:31:41,838
[♪ music continues]

473
00:31:53,183 --> 00:31:54,643
[Kang] Uh-huh, I'm on it. Yes.

474
00:31:54,726 --> 00:31:56,311
I'll make sure I look into it. All right.

475
00:31:56,394 --> 00:31:58,313
[investigator] You can't
write the story like that.

476
00:31:59,773 --> 00:32:02,609
Hey, Miss Oh, um,
you wanna grab a drink? I wanted to--

477
00:32:11,660 --> 00:32:13,161
70 BILLION THROUGH BAEKHO
TRADING FROM 1974 TO 1979

478
00:32:14,371 --> 00:32:15,497
[knocks on door]

479
00:32:17,999 --> 00:32:19,084
[clears throat]

480
00:32:19,626 --> 00:32:20,752
Come in.

481
00:32:22,254 --> 00:32:24,047
Excuse me, sir, do you have a minute?

482
00:32:26,258 --> 00:32:27,550
What is it?

483
00:32:32,138 --> 00:32:33,181
[sighs]

484
00:32:33,265 --> 00:32:35,558
You settling in, Baek? Feel at home?

485
00:32:35,642 --> 00:32:37,310
Yes, sir. It's been fine.

486
00:32:44,651 --> 00:32:45,986
Baek Soyeong.

487
00:32:47,028 --> 00:32:48,905
I'll get a warrant to bring her in.

488
00:32:50,198 --> 00:32:52,492
[inhales deeply] Hold off for now.

489
00:32:53,743 --> 00:32:54,744
Why?

490
00:32:56,329 --> 00:32:57,330
Hold off.

491
00:32:58,081 --> 00:32:59,082
Why should I?

492
00:33:00,959 --> 00:33:02,711
Are you being difficult right now?

493
00:33:02,794 --> 00:33:05,171
Can you just try to explain your approach?

494
00:33:05,255 --> 00:33:07,382
Why am I supposed to stand down?

495
00:33:07,465 --> 00:33:09,509
Because you take orders from me!

496
00:33:10,260 --> 00:33:11,636
You are not…

497
00:33:13,430 --> 00:33:14,639
[inhales sharply]

498
00:33:16,141 --> 00:33:18,768
You are not doing anything
without my approval.

499
00:33:18,852 --> 00:33:19,936
But why?

500
00:33:21,521 --> 00:33:23,982
Don't tell me the higher-ups
are stopping you again.

501
00:33:26,776 --> 00:33:27,861
[Geonyoung sighs]

502
00:33:28,778 --> 00:33:31,031
Just focus on the slush fund for now.

503
00:33:31,573 --> 00:33:33,825
Our first priority is finding the ledger,

504
00:33:33,908 --> 00:33:35,201
then we go for Cheon,

505
00:33:35,702 --> 00:33:37,078
and finally, Baek Kitae.

506
00:33:39,205 --> 00:33:40,415
[sighs]

507
00:33:40,915 --> 00:33:41,958
[lighter flicks open]

508
00:33:42,751 --> 00:33:44,627
All right, let me ask you something.

509
00:33:46,171 --> 00:33:48,089
Are you sure going this far is…

510
00:33:48,965 --> 00:33:50,050
responsible?

511
00:33:51,384 --> 00:33:52,552
[lighter closes]

512
00:33:53,094 --> 00:33:54,387
[thuds]

513
00:33:54,471 --> 00:33:55,513
Say more.

514
00:33:55,597 --> 00:33:57,640
Look, going after Baek is one thing.

515
00:33:58,183 --> 00:34:00,143
Torturing prisoners is something else.

516
00:34:01,603 --> 00:34:03,396
I know times have changed and everything.

517
00:34:04,898 --> 00:34:06,733
But everyone deserves dignity.

518
00:34:07,484 --> 00:34:09,402
People deserve basic human rights.

519
00:34:10,153 --> 00:34:13,740
[shouting] You saying I should feel guilty
for the way I handle a bunch of animals?

520
00:34:16,993 --> 00:34:19,788
Is that it?
You want to go back to the old days?

521
00:34:22,540 --> 00:34:24,459
Tell me what you want from me.

522
00:34:25,585 --> 00:34:28,171
How is it that becoming a prosecutor
didn't change you one bit?

523
00:34:30,215 --> 00:34:32,884
The country is being turned upside down.

524
00:34:36,429 --> 00:34:37,597
Yeah, what about you?

525
00:34:39,140 --> 00:34:40,975
Because you've obviously changed.

526
00:34:45,271 --> 00:34:46,439
Get out.

527
00:34:48,858 --> 00:34:50,026
Go on.

528
00:34:50,110 --> 00:34:52,112
[♪ somber music playing]

529
00:35:02,288 --> 00:35:03,373
[door slams]

530
00:35:04,040 --> 00:35:05,208
[sighs]

531
00:35:13,758 --> 00:35:17,470
BAEKHO TRADING INC.

532
00:35:26,896 --> 00:35:29,607
[Kang huffs] What the hell? Shit.

533
00:35:30,191 --> 00:35:31,526
I guess they're closed.

534
00:35:36,448 --> 00:35:37,866
Hey, where'd you say she lived?

535
00:35:38,825 --> 00:35:40,076
Remember,

536
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:43,163
we're getting meat delivered today,
so marinate some bulgogi.

537
00:35:43,246 --> 00:35:46,583
And either throw the abalone out
or take it home. It's not fresh.

538
00:35:47,125 --> 00:35:49,210
Oh, and get the snacks ready
for Minju on time for once.

539
00:35:49,294 --> 00:35:50,670
Yes, ma'am.

540
00:35:52,630 --> 00:35:53,798
Wow.

541
00:35:54,841 --> 00:35:55,967
Is that <i>hanbok</i> new?

542
00:35:57,844 --> 00:35:59,387
It's been a long time, Miss Baek.

543
00:35:59,471 --> 00:36:00,889
How's your daughter been?

544
00:36:05,435 --> 00:36:07,312
PROSECUTOR OH YEJIN

545
00:36:07,395 --> 00:36:08,438
[scoffs]

546
00:36:09,439 --> 00:36:10,732
A prosecutor?

547
00:36:12,859 --> 00:36:14,110
Well, look who's moving up.

548
00:36:14,778 --> 00:36:15,904
I know, right?

549
00:36:17,155 --> 00:36:19,115
I even get to eat pineapple now.

550
00:36:19,699 --> 00:36:21,367
Mmm. That's tasty.

551
00:36:24,412 --> 00:36:25,622
Why'd you come to my house today?

552
00:36:26,664 --> 00:36:27,665
[Yejin] Mmm.

553
00:36:28,792 --> 00:36:30,376
Well, the factory was closed, so,

554
00:36:31,753 --> 00:36:34,005
I stopped by your home,
hoping you'd be around

555
00:36:34,088 --> 00:36:35,089
'cause I missed you.

556
00:36:36,549 --> 00:36:40,136
You know the meth operation at…
Baekho Trading?

557
00:36:40,220 --> 00:36:41,221
[Soyeong scoffs]

558
00:36:42,096 --> 00:36:44,432
What are you talking about? [sighs]

559
00:36:45,892 --> 00:36:46,893
You drunk right now?

560
00:36:47,519 --> 00:36:49,229
Why did you close up shop there?

561
00:36:49,854 --> 00:36:51,606
I bet your brother told you to.

562
00:36:51,689 --> 00:36:54,234
Slow down.
You do know who my brother is, right?

563
00:36:54,818 --> 00:36:57,320
-Director of the KCIA.
-Whoa.

564
00:36:57,403 --> 00:36:59,614
You really think
you can threaten me, bitch?

565
00:36:59,697 --> 00:37:01,366
You're a two-bit prosecutor.

566
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:04,035
[laughing]

567
00:37:04,536 --> 00:37:05,954
[fork clatters]

568
00:37:14,671 --> 00:37:16,297
[Soyeong breathing heavily]

569
00:37:16,381 --> 00:37:19,717
You're turning into a junkie trying
to clean up after your brother, huh?

570
00:37:19,801 --> 00:37:21,553
-Let go!
-Baek Soyeong, listen.

571
00:37:21,636 --> 00:37:24,264
You know your brother's department
is weak now.

572
00:37:24,347 --> 00:37:27,642
So get your head on straight
before you wind up in a world of hurt.

573
00:37:28,685 --> 00:37:30,144
You know Choi Yuji, right?

574
00:37:30,228 --> 00:37:33,690
She's locked up at the Joint Investigation
Headquarters right now. [scoffs]

575
00:37:35,775 --> 00:37:38,319
You wanna stay out of prison
with your brother, right?

576
00:37:38,820 --> 00:37:40,238
Then I'd talk if I were you.

577
00:37:40,321 --> 00:37:41,906
Screw you.

578
00:37:41,990 --> 00:37:43,366
Aren't you still a mother?

579
00:37:44,701 --> 00:37:47,704
For your daughter's sake,
get off the junk already.

580
00:37:48,329 --> 00:37:50,373
[sighs] Ugh, geez.

581
00:37:52,125 --> 00:37:54,127
[Soyeong breathing heavily]

582
00:37:59,257 --> 00:38:01,968
-[door opens]
-I hate that little shit.

583
00:38:02,051 --> 00:38:03,344
-[door closes]
-Hey, come here!

584
00:38:03,428 --> 00:38:05,179
Throw some salt outside!

585
00:38:05,263 --> 00:38:06,264
[whispers] Damn it.

586
00:38:08,683 --> 00:38:10,518
[breathes heavily] Oh.

587
00:38:12,437 --> 00:38:13,897
[chuckles awkwardly]

588
00:38:15,189 --> 00:38:16,316
Minju, there you are.

589
00:38:17,317 --> 00:38:18,860
Let's have a snack. Come here.

590
00:38:21,070 --> 00:38:22,488
Hurry, let's go.

591
00:38:26,534 --> 00:38:28,786
[breathes deeply]

592
00:38:29,954 --> 00:38:30,955
[Yejin] <i>I was right.</i>

593
00:38:31,039 --> 00:38:32,040
-<i>Soyeong's an addict.</i>
-Shit.

594
00:38:32,123 --> 00:38:33,750
Start tracking down the other members.

595
00:38:33,833 --> 00:38:36,961
Yeah, but Jang told us
our priority should be the slush fund.

596
00:38:37,045 --> 00:38:38,755
You sure this is okay?

597
00:38:38,838 --> 00:38:40,840
Look, Baek's my target
for drug trafficking.

598
00:38:41,549 --> 00:38:43,635
He's the reason I wound up in Seoul.

599
00:38:44,344 --> 00:38:45,970
Right, let's go.

600
00:38:47,972 --> 00:38:50,600
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

601
00:39:04,656 --> 00:39:06,074
Have you two met before today?

602
00:39:06,741 --> 00:39:08,785
Yes, we met one time, briefly.

603
00:39:08,868 --> 00:39:10,828
When the president was still alive.

604
00:39:13,122 --> 00:39:14,874
By the way, Director Baek,

605
00:39:14,958 --> 00:39:18,252
I can sense you're blessed
with remarkably good energy.

606
00:39:18,962 --> 00:39:20,129
Thank you, ma'am.

607
00:39:22,131 --> 00:39:25,093
You two only met once
and she still recognizes you.

608
00:39:25,677 --> 00:39:26,886
I assume he…

609
00:39:27,804 --> 00:39:29,555
he must've made quite an impression.

610
00:39:30,181 --> 00:39:32,058
Well, I suppose, I just

611
00:39:33,893 --> 00:39:37,605
look at someone and say what I'm seeing.

612
00:39:39,273 --> 00:39:41,567
Madam Shin worked
for the president. [sighs]

613
00:39:42,443 --> 00:39:45,780
When he was in office,
she helped with a lot of major decisions.

614
00:39:48,908 --> 00:39:50,868
She and I are quite close as well.

615
00:39:52,912 --> 00:39:54,455
Oh. I see.

616
00:39:54,539 --> 00:39:55,873
Okay, so,

617
00:39:57,000 --> 00:40:00,044
the woman that's in prison,
you mentioned she's Japanese?

618
00:40:00,128 --> 00:40:01,129
[Kitae] Yes.

619
00:40:01,838 --> 00:40:03,923
She's originally <i>Zainichi</i> Korean,

620
00:40:04,841 --> 00:40:06,759
but she managed
to get citizenship in Japan.

621
00:40:06,843 --> 00:40:10,263
Well, then, I should speak
to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

622
00:40:12,140 --> 00:40:15,810
If you end up getting involved personally,
it'll be a bad look for everyone.

623
00:40:17,895 --> 00:40:19,439
Well, since I've been having problems

624
00:40:19,522 --> 00:40:21,774
thanks to the pricks
over at the JIH lately.

625
00:40:22,400 --> 00:40:23,443
[Kitae sighs]

626
00:40:24,360 --> 00:40:26,904
I'm sure Director Baek can
handle the ledger on his own.

627
00:40:29,991 --> 00:40:32,744
Would you work with me for a while
to help resolve some of these issues?

628
00:40:35,496 --> 00:40:36,914
What, for free?

629
00:40:36,998 --> 00:40:38,249
[scoffs]

630
00:40:39,333 --> 00:40:42,545
Come on, I'm not Hwang.
I don't expect any free favors.

631
00:40:42,628 --> 00:40:46,215
You'll be well compensated
if things go off without a hitch.

632
00:40:46,299 --> 00:40:48,301
[laughing]

633
00:40:51,345 --> 00:40:53,431
Don't worry, it was just a joke.

634
00:40:54,724 --> 00:40:56,350
You seem a little on edge today.

635
00:40:56,976 --> 00:40:59,687
Truth is, it really wouldn't
make a difference anyway.

636
00:40:59,771 --> 00:41:02,899
It's all in the name
of our country, isn't it?

637
00:41:03,524 --> 00:41:04,525
[chuckles]

638
00:41:05,943 --> 00:41:07,278
In any case,

639
00:41:07,904 --> 00:41:12,241
I'll pray nice and hard for both of you
from today onward, all right?

640
00:41:16,162 --> 00:41:17,163
[chuckles]

641
00:41:20,625 --> 00:41:22,168
All right, turn your head a little.

642
00:41:22,835 --> 00:41:25,004
Mmm, a little further to the right.

643
00:41:25,088 --> 00:41:26,380
[shutter clicks]

644
00:41:27,632 --> 00:41:28,883
[in Japanese] Thanks.

645
00:41:32,053 --> 00:41:33,513
[phone rings]

646
00:41:34,597 --> 00:41:36,265
[in English] This is Baek Kihyun.

647
00:41:36,349 --> 00:41:37,558
[Kitae] <i>You joined the JIH?</i>

648
00:41:37,642 --> 00:41:39,936
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

649
00:41:40,019 --> 00:41:41,020
Yes.

650
00:41:41,104 --> 00:41:42,647
[sighs]

651
00:41:42,730 --> 00:41:44,524
How come you didn't say anything?

652
00:41:45,691 --> 00:41:47,151
<i>I was going to.</i>

653
00:41:49,695 --> 00:41:52,782
Jang Geonyoung's working there
as a special consultant, huh?

654
00:41:53,950 --> 00:41:54,951
Yes.

655
00:41:58,412 --> 00:42:00,331
Ahn put in a good word for him, I guess.

656
00:42:00,414 --> 00:42:03,501
<i>They're from the same town,</i>
<i>went to the same high school.</i>

657
00:42:03,584 --> 00:42:06,254
These small town connections. Damn it.

658
00:42:08,631 --> 00:42:11,300
[sighs] Don't get comfortable over there.

659
00:42:12,176 --> 00:42:14,137
Jang Geonyoung specifically chose you

660
00:42:14,220 --> 00:42:17,390
<i>because he wants to mess with your head.</i>
<i>You understand?</i>

661
00:42:18,558 --> 00:42:19,684
Yeah. I'm aware.

662
00:42:20,393 --> 00:42:21,811
[Jaeho] About Colonel Baek…

663
00:42:23,521 --> 00:42:25,273
Shouldn't we get ahead of this?

664
00:42:26,232 --> 00:42:28,109
How long you plan to let him be?

665
00:42:28,943 --> 00:42:30,194
I could talk to him.

666
00:42:31,195 --> 00:42:32,321
Just leave him alone.

667
00:42:33,156 --> 00:42:35,241
All these eyes on him, it won't be long.

668
00:42:35,324 --> 00:42:37,994
He'll figure it out. He's not a child.

669
00:42:38,619 --> 00:42:39,954
You think Baek would

670
00:42:40,496 --> 00:42:41,998
betray his own brother?

671
00:42:44,083 --> 00:42:46,377
Let's wait a bit longer
and see what he chooses.

672
00:42:47,253 --> 00:42:50,298
He either goes down with his brother,
or he survives with us.

673
00:42:51,757 --> 00:42:53,342
<i>How's Choi Yuji holding up?</i>

674
00:42:56,137 --> 00:42:59,140
Pretty good for now, I guess,
but it'll get worse.

675
00:42:59,724 --> 00:43:01,267
Believe me, she's solid.

676
00:43:02,143 --> 00:43:03,394
All you have to do

677
00:43:03,978 --> 00:43:06,314
is keep an eye on Jang
and report to me afterward.

678
00:43:07,732 --> 00:43:08,733
Yeah. I'm on it.

679
00:43:10,067 --> 00:43:11,319
What about Soyeong?

680
00:43:11,944 --> 00:43:13,738
Is she gonna be okay or what?

681
00:43:14,780 --> 00:43:17,700
<i>Don't worry about that.</i>
<i>She's not their target anyway.</i>

682
00:43:18,618 --> 00:43:19,827
Yes, sir. Copy that.

683
00:43:21,495 --> 00:43:22,705
[Geonyoung] Colonel Baek,

684
00:43:23,748 --> 00:43:24,916
you heading home yet?

685
00:43:24,999 --> 00:43:28,085
I've got a few things to do.
I'm just gonna finish up first.

686
00:43:28,169 --> 00:43:30,922
But it's getting late.
How about you finish in the morning?

687
00:43:31,422 --> 00:43:33,716
Soju sound good?
I'm buying the first round.

688
00:43:34,383 --> 00:43:35,384
Sounds great.

689
00:43:35,468 --> 00:43:37,845
How about some dwaeji gukbap
and some makgeolli?

690
00:43:37,929 --> 00:43:40,014
You should head home, Colonel Ahn.

691
00:43:40,097 --> 00:43:42,016
Your family's waiting. [chuckles]

692
00:43:42,099 --> 00:43:43,142
I think

693
00:43:43,893 --> 00:43:45,269
it's just gonna be us.

694
00:43:47,355 --> 00:43:49,357
-Okay, sure.
-All right.

695
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:51,275
-I'll be waiting outside.
-Great.

696
00:44:03,079 --> 00:44:04,664
[grunts]

697
00:44:08,501 --> 00:44:11,754
The memories are all rushing back to me,
sitting here with you.

698
00:44:11,837 --> 00:44:15,174
One night I was at this same table,
but I was with your brother.

699
00:44:15,716 --> 00:44:18,344
We had a bottle of soju, just like this.

700
00:44:19,637 --> 00:44:21,555
And we were here, eating dwaeji gukbap,

701
00:44:22,598 --> 00:44:23,975
on a rainy night like tonight.

702
00:44:28,187 --> 00:44:29,730
What is it you want from me?

703
00:44:33,859 --> 00:44:35,278
Not much, to be honest.

704
00:44:35,987 --> 00:44:39,198
Well, actually, there is one thing.

705
00:44:39,282 --> 00:44:40,700
It's not a big deal.

706
00:44:40,783 --> 00:44:42,118
Sorry, would you, um,

707
00:44:42,785 --> 00:44:45,204
mind if I speak candidly
with you from now on?

708
00:44:45,830 --> 00:44:46,998
After all, we're a team now.

709
00:44:49,500 --> 00:44:51,002
We are a team, aren't we?

710
00:44:52,253 --> 00:44:54,714
Oh, of course. Be candid.

711
00:44:55,464 --> 00:44:56,882
[chuckling] I knew it.

712
00:44:57,550 --> 00:45:00,428
You're just like your brother.
The boss man.

713
00:45:00,511 --> 00:45:02,054
You're just as much
of a big shot as he is.

714
00:45:04,682 --> 00:45:06,684
Here you go. Let me pour you a drink.

715
00:45:07,727 --> 00:45:09,729
Look, stop beating around the bush.

716
00:45:10,646 --> 00:45:12,398
Why'd you bring me into the JIH?

717
00:45:13,274 --> 00:45:14,317
[chuckles]

718
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:17,570
[sighs]

719
00:45:27,038 --> 00:45:28,831
Use your head and look alive.

720
00:45:29,665 --> 00:45:31,625
Okay, what exactly does that mean?

721
00:45:31,709 --> 00:45:33,919
You're better off taking it at face value.

722
00:45:34,420 --> 00:45:36,756
Just do your best to see things
as they are.

723
00:45:37,506 --> 00:45:38,966
You're in a different world now.

724
00:45:41,052 --> 00:45:42,845
You can't keep living
like you always have.

725
00:45:42,928 --> 00:45:44,221
[scoffs]

726
00:45:46,724 --> 00:45:48,100
So I'm supposed to…

727
00:45:48,893 --> 00:45:50,603
to betray my own brother?

728
00:45:52,772 --> 00:45:53,856
[glass thuds]

729
00:45:55,441 --> 00:45:56,442
Minju.

730
00:45:58,861 --> 00:46:00,488
Who's gonna raise her?

731
00:46:01,322 --> 00:46:02,865
Are you willing to do that

732
00:46:03,449 --> 00:46:05,451
if Baek Soyeong goes to jail?

733
00:46:07,411 --> 00:46:08,496
[scoffs]

734
00:46:08,579 --> 00:46:10,581
[♪ tense music playing]

735
00:46:13,084 --> 00:46:14,502
[grunts]

736
00:46:17,296 --> 00:46:19,090
The truth is, uh…

737
00:46:22,676 --> 00:46:25,554
that your family complicates things
all the time, right?

738
00:46:25,638 --> 00:46:29,016
If you want your sister to live
and your niece to have a normal childhood,

739
00:46:30,893 --> 00:46:33,270
you have to ensure you survive first.

740
00:46:36,065 --> 00:46:37,274
What do you want?

741
00:46:38,401 --> 00:46:39,819
What do I have to do?

742
00:46:41,779 --> 00:46:44,990
Make sure you keep an eye
on Baek Kitae's activities.

743
00:46:45,616 --> 00:46:47,701
Watch him and find out what he's planning.

744
00:46:49,787 --> 00:46:51,956
You think your brother's gonna sit still?

745
00:46:52,832 --> 00:46:54,750
He's going to try something.

746
00:46:56,877 --> 00:46:58,379
[drink pouring]

747
00:46:59,755 --> 00:47:01,549
You're in hell right now, aren't you?

748
00:47:03,217 --> 00:47:05,886
You want to escape that
and get your life back?

749
00:47:08,764 --> 00:47:09,765
Choice is yours.

750
00:47:11,475 --> 00:47:12,601
Pick a side.

751
00:47:16,689 --> 00:47:20,317
All right, then, how about we go elsewhere

752
00:47:21,402 --> 00:47:22,445
and get another round?

753
00:47:25,281 --> 00:47:27,032
This weather makes me thirsty.

754
00:47:27,867 --> 00:47:29,118
Mmm.

755
00:47:34,123 --> 00:47:35,332
Colonel Baek.

756
00:47:36,584 --> 00:47:37,877
See you tomorrow.

757
00:47:50,139 --> 00:47:51,640
[grunts]

758
00:47:59,398 --> 00:48:00,566
[sighs]

759
00:48:05,279 --> 00:48:08,115
♪ …<i>toy train goes chugging along </i>♪

760
00:48:08,199 --> 00:48:11,452
♪ <i>Carrying cookies and candy</i> ♪

761
00:48:11,535 --> 00:48:14,288
[sighs] Kitae, what on earth is going on?

762
00:48:16,916 --> 00:48:18,542
-The lab. Did you shut it down?
-Mm-hmm.

763
00:48:18,626 --> 00:48:21,003
I moved everything out after you called.

764
00:48:21,086 --> 00:48:23,088
All right, tell the others
to keep their mouths shut

765
00:48:23,172 --> 00:48:24,548
and stay away from there for a while.

766
00:48:25,424 --> 00:48:28,677
Wait, but don't tell me we're gonna
stop production for good. Are we?

767
00:48:28,761 --> 00:48:30,513
No, we won't be shutting down.
Why would we?

768
00:48:31,388 --> 00:48:33,349
We'll ramp back up
once things settle down.

769
00:48:33,432 --> 00:48:34,433
How long?

770
00:48:36,393 --> 00:48:37,770
Just wait.

771
00:48:39,104 --> 00:48:40,940
First, I have to take back
what they stole.

772
00:48:41,023 --> 00:48:42,566
But what did they steal?

773
00:48:46,612 --> 00:48:49,949
♪ <i>To our baby in Mom's room</i> ♪

774
00:48:53,077 --> 00:48:55,120
Have a good day, Uncle Kitae.

775
00:48:55,704 --> 00:48:56,914
[Kitae] All right.

776
00:49:00,751 --> 00:49:02,086
[Soyeong sighs, grunts]

777
00:49:02,169 --> 00:49:05,214
♪ <i>The little toy train</i>
<i>Goes chugging along--</i> ♪

778
00:49:05,297 --> 00:49:06,924
Go play somewhere else!

779
00:49:07,550 --> 00:49:08,968
[sighs] Shit.

780
00:49:10,219 --> 00:49:12,763
[breathing heavily]

781
00:49:15,599 --> 00:49:17,560
-[door opens]
-[footsteps approach]

782
00:49:17,643 --> 00:49:19,270
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

783
00:49:19,353 --> 00:49:20,813
Sir, I've got some news.

784
00:49:21,772 --> 00:49:22,815
What is it?

785
00:49:23,566 --> 00:49:25,776
A notice from
the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

786
00:49:28,779 --> 00:49:30,155
NOTICE REGARDING
DETAINED ZAINICHI KOREAN

787
00:49:30,239 --> 00:49:32,491
[Jaeho] The Japanese government
has lodged a formal complaint.

788
00:49:32,575 --> 00:49:34,994
We also heard from
the Martial Law Command.

789
00:49:35,077 --> 00:49:38,330
They both want Ikeda Yuji released,
effective immediately.

790
00:49:38,414 --> 00:49:39,873
[phone rings]

791
00:49:41,458 --> 00:49:44,169
-Yeah?
-<i>Mr. Jang, this is the guard post.</i>

792
00:49:44,253 --> 00:49:46,005
<i>Your sister is here to see you, sir.</i>

793
00:49:47,047 --> 00:49:48,173
Put her on.

794
00:49:56,015 --> 00:49:58,475
Excuse me. Where's
the Joint Investigation Headquarters?

795
00:49:58,559 --> 00:50:00,644
Oh, the JIH? It's right over there.

796
00:50:00,728 --> 00:50:02,354
-Oh, thank you.
-Sure.

797
00:50:07,276 --> 00:50:09,278
[phone ringing in distance]

798
00:50:25,461 --> 00:50:28,172
-How can I help you?
-Uh…

799
00:50:31,759 --> 00:50:33,260
[Geonyoung] Hyeeun.

800
00:50:33,344 --> 00:50:34,762
Oh, good morning.

801
00:50:35,429 --> 00:50:36,639
Come on in.

802
00:50:39,433 --> 00:50:41,769
I should introduce you to Colonel Baek.

803
00:50:41,852 --> 00:50:44,104
He and I have been working together.
Say hello.

804
00:50:45,022 --> 00:50:47,566
Right. Hello. Jang Hyeeun, sir.

805
00:50:48,817 --> 00:50:50,319
She's my sister.

806
00:50:52,738 --> 00:50:54,239
Baek Kihyun, Miss Jang.

807
00:50:56,784 --> 00:50:58,077
Let's go.

808
00:51:03,791 --> 00:51:06,669
I've heard so much
about this department lately.

809
00:51:07,336 --> 00:51:09,505
The JIH has been all over the news.

810
00:51:10,923 --> 00:51:12,299
So how have you been doing?

811
00:51:13,175 --> 00:51:15,010
You know, same as usual.

812
00:51:19,682 --> 00:51:22,017
What about you? Are you doing okay?

813
00:51:24,228 --> 00:51:25,479
[chuckles softly]

814
00:51:25,562 --> 00:51:27,106
Yeah, everything's fine.

815
00:51:28,482 --> 00:51:29,692
Why do you ask?

816
00:51:31,276 --> 00:51:32,861
You're thin and pale, Geonyoung.

817
00:51:34,321 --> 00:51:35,614
I'm getting worried about you.

818
00:51:36,657 --> 00:51:38,409
I've been busy, that's all.

819
00:51:38,492 --> 00:51:39,702
Don't worry, I'm okay.

820
00:51:42,621 --> 00:51:45,332
[inhales deeply] Hyeeun.

821
00:51:46,208 --> 00:51:48,127
I'm not the same man I used to be.

822
00:51:49,962 --> 00:51:51,004
You don't

823
00:51:52,005 --> 00:51:53,924
need to worry about me, all right?

824
00:51:57,761 --> 00:52:00,097
But I still do. I can't help it.

825
00:52:00,180 --> 00:52:01,223
[sobbing]

826
00:52:06,311 --> 00:52:07,521
[Geonyoung sighs]

827
00:52:08,397 --> 00:52:11,150
-[phone ringing]
-[sniffling, sobbing]

828
00:52:15,904 --> 00:52:17,698
Hey, let me call you right back.

829
00:52:17,781 --> 00:52:19,783
[Hyeeun crying]

830
00:52:19,867 --> 00:52:22,619
Sorry. I'm being silly.

831
00:52:25,164 --> 00:52:26,498
I almost forgot.

832
00:52:27,833 --> 00:52:30,836
Here are some leftovers
from Dad's funeral yesterday.

833
00:52:30,919 --> 00:52:32,254
You should eat some of it.

834
00:52:37,259 --> 00:52:39,136
I wish I'd been with you.

835
00:52:39,970 --> 00:52:41,221
I'm really sorry.

836
00:52:44,141 --> 00:52:45,642
It must've been hard on your own.

837
00:52:45,726 --> 00:52:47,561
Uh, not at all actually.

838
00:52:47,644 --> 00:52:49,980
-[phone ringing]
-[Hyeeun chuckles]

839
00:52:56,695 --> 00:52:57,696
Yes?

840
00:52:58,322 --> 00:52:59,782
Yeah, I'll be there soon.

841
00:53:00,866 --> 00:53:02,284
[radio host] <i>…will mostly be clear.</i>

842
00:53:02,367 --> 00:53:03,911
-[grunts]
-[gasping]

843
00:53:03,994 --> 00:53:06,371
[radio host] <i>…slightly lower</i>
<i>than yesterday, so it'll feel chilly.</i>

844
00:53:06,455 --> 00:53:08,582
<i>In Seoul, we're looking at a low</i>
<i>of 3 degrees Celsius…</i>

845
00:53:08,665 --> 00:53:10,417
-[radio turns off]
-[Yuji gasps]

846
00:53:11,585 --> 00:53:12,878
[Geonyoung] Bring her here.

847
00:53:13,837 --> 00:53:15,839
[Yuji gasping]

848
00:53:16,965 --> 00:53:18,383
[grunting]

849
00:53:19,426 --> 00:53:20,427
[coughs]

850
00:53:21,136 --> 00:53:23,096
[wheezing, panting]

851
00:53:35,943 --> 00:53:37,402
[investigator] Got her? [grunts]

852
00:53:37,486 --> 00:53:39,488
[Yuji breathing raggedly]

853
00:53:48,956 --> 00:53:50,541
Everyone out.

854
00:53:56,213 --> 00:53:57,464
[Yuji shivering]

855
00:53:59,466 --> 00:54:00,884
[Geonyoung] Choi Yuji.

856
00:54:00,968 --> 00:54:02,845
-[shivering]
-Choi Yuji!

857
00:54:04,596 --> 00:54:06,598
-[door closes]
-[continues shivering]

858
00:54:08,809 --> 00:54:12,980
We were contacted by the Japanese
Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

859
00:54:13,647 --> 00:54:15,148
It says right here…

860
00:54:17,401 --> 00:54:18,694
they want you released immediately.

861
00:54:18,777 --> 00:54:20,779
[Yuji breathing heavily]

862
00:54:24,575 --> 00:54:26,577
[♪ tense music playing]

863
00:54:31,081 --> 00:54:32,374
[Geonyoung sighs]

864
00:54:32,457 --> 00:54:34,167
You think I'm gonna
let you walk out of here

865
00:54:35,127 --> 00:54:37,254
because of some official document? Huh?

866
00:54:43,427 --> 00:54:45,220
[breathing shakily]

867
00:54:46,722 --> 00:54:49,474
-Tell me where the ledger is.
-[breathing heavily]

868
00:54:49,558 --> 00:54:53,020
Tell me where it is! Where is it? Come on!

869
00:54:53,103 --> 00:54:56,398
Answer me or you're dead.
Where's the ledger?

870
00:54:56,481 --> 00:54:59,526
Say it! Where is it?

871
00:55:00,152 --> 00:55:03,238
[Kihun] <i>Director Baek,</i>
<i>I found Takahashi Kazuo.</i>

872
00:55:04,114 --> 00:55:05,157
Where is he?

873
00:55:05,240 --> 00:55:07,534
Busan Hotel. Room 308.

874
00:55:07,618 --> 00:55:09,369
Listen, stay until I get there.

875
00:55:09,911 --> 00:55:11,788
-I'm on the way now.
-<i>Yes, sir.</i>

876
00:55:12,372 --> 00:55:14,541
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

877
00:56:13,308 --> 00:56:16,436
-[Kitae] Where's the ledger?
-[♪ music continues]

878
00:56:25,737 --> 00:56:27,572
What happened to the <i>kumicho</i>?

879
00:56:28,073 --> 00:56:30,075
We'll get her out soon, trust me on that.

880
00:56:30,826 --> 00:56:34,579
Until then, I'm gonna need you
to hand over the slush fund ledger.

881
00:56:35,539 --> 00:56:37,249
The <i>kumicho</i> said

882
00:56:37,332 --> 00:56:39,209
that I shouldn't give it to anyone.

883
00:56:40,961 --> 00:56:42,754
I already talked to Choi Yuji.

884
00:56:43,505 --> 00:56:45,966
I won't be able to get her out
unless you hand it over.

885
00:56:47,092 --> 00:56:49,761
You know what happens
if that ledger gets picked up by the JIH?

886
00:56:49,845 --> 00:56:52,013
All of us are going down.

887
00:56:52,097 --> 00:56:53,724
[♪ music continues]

888
00:57:12,617 --> 00:57:13,994
[brakes screech]

889
00:57:33,638 --> 00:57:34,931
[Kazuo] Hang on.

890
00:57:37,267 --> 00:57:40,312
You mean you and the <i>kumicho</i>
had a conversation recently?

891
00:57:41,563 --> 00:57:45,192
The JIH took her into custody,
put her in some prison to torture her.

892
00:57:46,568 --> 00:57:48,612
How could you have talked to her?

893
00:57:49,738 --> 00:57:53,033
Oh, you know,
you really ask too many questions.

894
00:57:55,619 --> 00:57:56,828
[grunting]

895
00:58:04,461 --> 00:58:06,213
[groans]

896
00:58:08,548 --> 00:58:09,800
[grunts]

897
00:58:10,926 --> 00:58:12,511
[groans]

898
00:58:12,594 --> 00:58:14,638
[breath trembling]

899
00:58:22,938 --> 00:58:24,356
[grunts]

900
00:58:25,565 --> 00:58:26,983
Bastard.

901
00:58:27,067 --> 00:58:28,777
[panting]

902
00:58:28,860 --> 00:58:30,529
[♪ dramatic music playing]

903
00:59:00,517 --> 00:59:02,185
-Move!
-[housekeeper exclaims]

904
00:59:02,269 --> 00:59:03,353
[screams]

905
00:59:07,148 --> 00:59:09,442
[Kitae breathing heavily] Oh, shit.

906
00:59:13,280 --> 00:59:15,240
-[gunshots]
-[housekeeper yelps]

907
00:59:15,323 --> 00:59:17,158
[Kitae breathing heavily]

908
00:59:18,618 --> 00:59:20,161
[♪ music continues]

909
00:59:20,245 --> 00:59:21,663
[breathing heavily]

910
00:59:28,295 --> 00:59:29,504
[Geonyoung] Move!

911
00:59:40,098 --> 00:59:42,475
-[breathing heavily]
-[grunts]

912
00:59:56,406 --> 00:59:57,949
[breathing heavily]

913
01:00:12,380 --> 01:00:13,506
[breathing heavily]

914
01:00:17,177 --> 01:00:19,179
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

915
01:00:29,814 --> 01:00:32,776
[sighs] Well, Mr. Jang.

916
01:00:33,526 --> 01:00:35,111
You did a bang-up job here.

917
01:00:36,321 --> 01:00:38,198
Now that you've seen it,
what do you think?

918
01:00:38,281 --> 01:00:40,116
[chuckling]

919
01:00:42,285 --> 01:00:44,120
I think

920
01:00:44,204 --> 01:00:48,083
every single one of those pricks
is gonna wind up behind bars.

921
01:01:00,887 --> 01:01:02,347
That old geezer.

922
01:01:04,891 --> 01:01:06,518
He really held on, didn't he?

923
01:01:08,103 --> 01:01:10,897
Eighteen damn years in this chair.

924
01:01:13,692 --> 01:01:16,444
And just when I thought
it was finally my turn…

925
01:01:20,490 --> 01:01:21,783
Goddamn it.

926
01:01:23,660 --> 01:01:26,663
Looks like that bald asshole
Hwang is gonna take it.

927
01:01:29,416 --> 01:01:31,251
So, Kitae.

928
01:01:32,127 --> 01:01:33,128
Yes, sir.

929
01:01:33,712 --> 01:01:35,588
What are you gonna do now?

930
01:01:38,133 --> 01:01:39,134
Huh?

931
01:01:41,177 --> 01:01:42,262
Hey.

932
01:01:45,181 --> 01:01:47,058
You just gonna go down like this?

933
01:01:52,605 --> 01:01:54,983
There's something
I'd like your approval for.

934
01:01:55,066 --> 01:01:56,401
It's very important.

935
01:01:59,779 --> 01:02:00,822
Hwang Daesik.

936
01:02:02,073 --> 01:02:04,367
I wanna take care of him.
I'll do it myself.

937
01:02:06,911 --> 01:02:08,872
You really think you can handle that?

938
01:02:09,956 --> 01:02:11,499
Oh, it would be my pleasure.

939
01:02:12,083 --> 01:02:14,419
I'll do it my own way.

940
01:02:18,590 --> 01:02:21,593
[♪ intriguing music playing]

